# Wren Featherfoot's camp talks (story/camp_talk.gd): offered after a Long Rest once the opening `if` holds; each
# plays once. Quest: The Last Lesson (narrative/companions/lesson.dialogue). The file offers its first talk that
# holds: when he's Strained or Doubtful (story/approval.gd), those first; then the quest's; then Warm, Close and
# Devoted.

# --- When he's lost faith in the party (approval) ----------------------------------------------------------------

~ talk_strained
if name:wren_featherfoot and approval.wren_featherfoot <= strained
-> strained
endif
-> END

~ strained
Narrator: Wren is very calm tonight. No jokes, no handstands, no last word. He sits by the fire and speaks quietly, and that's how you know.
interject name:wren_featherfoot: I'm going to say this once, plainly, because I don't do plainly and I want you to notice.
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Master Sorrel took me off the street because he thought there was something in me worth the trouble. Lately I've been wondering what he'd make of the company I keep. I don't like the answer.
interject name:wren_featherfoot: I'll keep walking with you. I owe you that. But when it comes to the castle, and whatever's waiting for me up there, I'll be making my own choices. Not yours.
* Then help us earn your trust back. -> strained_earn
* We're sorry, Wren. -> strained_sorry
* That's your loss. -> strained_cold

~ strained_earn
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Easy, then. Be kind when it's stupid to be. Be kind when nobody would know. That's the trick.
interject name:wren_featherfoot: I'm still learning it myself. We can be terrible at it together.
approve wren_featherfoot +10: You asked how to earn my trust back
-> END

~ strained_sorry
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Noted. Sorry's a good start. Master Sorrel would say the leaf apologising to the wind changes nothing. Then he'd make tea anyway.
approve wren_featherfoot +5: You told me you were sorry
-> END

~ strained_cold
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Probably. Night.
approve wren_featherfoot -6: You told me it's my loss
-> END

~ talk_doubt
if name:wren_featherfoot and approval.wren_featherfoot == doubtful
-> doubt
endif
-> END

~ doubt
Narrator: Wren isn't doing handstands tonight. He's sitting on the boulder with his chin on his knees, which on Wren looks like a man in chains.
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Right. Quick one. I'll keep it short; I know you're all very busy being heroes.
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Master Sorrel had a saying. "Watch what your hands do when nobody's grading them." Lately our hands have been doing some things I'd not want graded.
interject name:wren_featherfoot: I was a thief, you know. I know what it looks like when somebody's talking themselves into something. I did it every day for years. It looks like this.
* Fair. We'll watch our hands. -> doubt_fair
* You'd know, thief. -> doubt_thief
* We're doing what has to be done. -> doubt_done

~ doubt_fair
interject name:wren_featherfoot: I'll allow it. ...Thanks. That was the sincere bit. Don't get used to it.
approve wren_featherfoot +6: You said we'd watch our hands
-> END

~ doubt_thief
Narrator: The joke he had ready doesn't come. He just looks at you.
interject name:wren_featherfoot: I would. That's why I'm saying it.
approve wren_featherfoot -4: You called me a thief for saying it
-> END

~ doubt_done
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Everybody says that. It was never once true when I said it.
approve wren_featherfoot +1: You told me we're doing what has to be done
-> END

# --- His quest ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

~ talk_sorrel
if name:wren_featherfoot and quest.the_last_lesson
-> sorrel
endif
-> END

~ sorrel
Narrator: Wren is doing a handstand on a boulder at the edge of the firelight. He has been doing it for some time. He doesn't seem tired.
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Evening. Don't mind me. Master Sorrel used to make me do this for an hour every night. Said it put the blood back where the brains were.
* Tell us about him. -> sorrel_tell
* How long can you do that? -> sorrel_long

~ sorrel_long
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Until someone asks me a question I don't want to answer. Then I fall over. It's very convenient.
-> sorrel_tell

~ sorrel_tell
Narrator: Wren comes down off his hands, neatly, and sits on the boulder with his knees up.
interject name:wren_featherfoot: I tried to pick his pocket. Big market day, old elf in grey, looked half asleep. He caught my wrist without turning round. Didn't even stop walking. Just walked me out of the market by the wrist, like a dog on a lead.
interject name:wren_featherfoot: He said, "You have very good hands and a very bad teacher. I can fix one of those." I said, which one. He said, "Come and find out."
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Fourteen years. A lesson a day. Some of them were punching. Most of them were sitting still, which is worse.
interject name:wren_featherfoot: He died before the last one. I asked him what it was, at the end. He said it was in the letter. And then he said, "Don't open it, you little thief." And then he laughed, and then he went.
* You never opened it? -> sorrel_never
* We'll find Kasimir. -> sorrel_find

~ sorrel_never
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Never. I've had it fourteen months in my shirt. I've held it up to candles. I'm a scoundrel, not a monster.
-> sorrel_find

~ sorrel_find
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Course we will. Easy. How many elves called Kasimir can there be in one valley? Don't answer that. It's a valley full of vampires; there's probably a club.
approve wren_featherfoot +1: You listened to me talk about Master Sorrel
-> END

~ talk_letter
if name:wren_featherfoot and quest.the_last_lesson >= the_brother
-> letter
endif
-> END

~ letter
Narrator: Wren is sitting very still at the fire tonight. It's the most unsettling thing you've seen him do.
interject name:wren_featherfoot: He had a sister. He had a brother and a sister and a mother and a whole people, and they were here, and he never said one word in fourteen years.
interject name:wren_featherfoot: I used to tell him everything. Every stupid thing. He'd just nod. I thought he didn't have anything to tell.
interject name:wren_featherfoot: "The boy who brings you this is the best thing I did with the time I stole." That's what he wrote. About me. I've been doing handstands for fourteen years and he thought I was the best thing he did.
* He was right. -> letter_right
* He wanted you to hear it from someone else. -> letter_else

~ letter_right
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Don't. Don't, I'll cry, and then you'll all have to watch a monk cry, and it's not a dignified sight. We cry with our whole bodies. It's all the flexibility.
approve wren_featherfoot +3: You told me Master Sorrel was right about me
-> letter_end

~ letter_else
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Sneaky. That's very him. He couldn't say it to my face. He wrote it down and posted it across a mountain range to make sure.
approve wren_featherfoot +2: You worked out why Master Sorrel wrote it down
-> letter_end

~ letter_end
interject name:wren_featherfoot: "Let her rest." That's what he told Kasimir. Let her rest. I think that's the lesson. I think. I'm not sure I've got it yet.
-> END

~ talk_rest
if name:wren_featherfoot and quest.the_last_lesson >= the_brother and not (quest.the_last_lesson >= let_her_rest) and (quest.patrinas_wail == at_rest or quest.patrinas_wail == destroyed or quest.patrinas_wail == restored)
-> rest
endif
-> END

~ rest
if quest.patrinas_wail == restored
Narrator: Wren comes back to the fire late, with his hands in his pockets, which he never does.
interject name:wren_featherfoot: She walked out of that temple barefoot in the snow and didn't look back once. Kasimir gave the thing in the grave every year he had but one, for that. He'll be dead by spring.
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Master Sorrel told him not to. He wrote it down and posted it across the mountains. Let her rest. And we got it there, and it wasn't enough.
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Maybe that's the lesson. That you can deliver the letter and it doesn't make anybody read it.
else
Narrator: Wren is sitting on the same boulder as always, not doing a handstand. He looks up as you come over.
interject name:wren_featherfoot: She's at rest. Patrina. Four hundred years of turning pages, and she closed the book. Kasimir said she looked surprised. Like she'd forgotten you were allowed to stop.
interject name:wren_featherfoot: So. That's done. Letter's delivered. I've been waiting all day to feel different. I keep stopping in doorways.
endif
interject name:wren_featherfoot: I don't feel finished. That's the thing. Master Sorrel said the last lesson was in the letter, and I've read the letter, well, I've heard it read, and I still don't know what the lesson was.
quest the_last_lesson let_her_rest
-> END

# --- As he comes to trust the party (approval) --------------------------------------------------------------------

~ talk_warm
if name:wren_featherfoot and approval.wren_featherfoot >= warm and level >= 3
-> warm
endif
-> END

~ warm
Narrator: Wren is juggling three stones, then four, then a stone, an apple and somebody's boot. It isn't clear whose boot.
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Evening. Don't look for your boot; it's in the air. Watch this.
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Master Sorrel used to say juggling's just throwing things and trusting they'll come back. I said that's not a lesson, that's optimism. He said those are the same thing, and caught all four without looking.
* Teach me. -> warm_teach
* Give me back my boot. -> warm_boot
* Do you ever stop moving? -> warm_stop

~ warm_teach
Narrator: Three stones. You drop nine, and catch one, and the one you catch is almost by accident.
interject name:wren_featherfoot: That one. That catch. Remember what your hands did. That's the whole of juggling, and most of everything else.
approve wren_featherfoot +3: You let me teach you to juggle
-> END

~ warm_boot
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Spoilsport. Here. It was getting heavy anyway; what have you got in there, a brick?
approve wren_featherfoot +1: You put up with me juggling your boot
-> END

~ warm_stop
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Only when I'm sad. So, no. Never. Look at me go.
Narrator: He catches everything, one-handed, and for a moment he's very still. Then the stones are up again.
approve wren_featherfoot +2: You asked whether I ever stop moving
-> END

~ talk_close
if name:wren_featherfoot and approval.wren_featherfoot >= close and level >= 5
-> close
endif
-> END

~ close
Narrator: It's late and quiet, and Wren is lying flat on his back in the grass, perfectly still. It takes you a moment to realise he isn't asleep.
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Don't panic. I'm practising sitting still. Master Sorrel said I'd never manage it. I'm proving him wrong after he's dead. It's very petty. He'd love it.
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Can I tell you the real thing? I'm scared I'm a clown with good knees. That I'm tricks all the way down, and if you took the jokes out there'd be nothing left but a halfling doing a handstand.
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Master Sorrel saw something in me. I've never known what. I've been too busy being funny to look.
* We've seen it too. -> close_seen
* The jokes are part of you. They're not a trick. -> close_part
* You don't have to be funny with us. -> close_funny

~ close_seen
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Have you? What does it look like? No, don't tell me. I'd only make a joke about it.
approve wren_featherfoot +3: You told me you've seen it too
-> close_end

~ close_part
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Huh. Part of me. Like a nose. A nose isn't a trick. A nose is a nose. I'll think about that.
approve wren_featherfoot +3: You told me the jokes are part of me
-> close_end

~ close_funny
interject name:wren_featherfoot: I know. That's what's so frightening about you lot. Everywhere else, being funny's the fee for being let in.
approve wren_featherfoot +3: You told me I don't have to be funny with you
-> close_end

~ close_end
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Right. Yes. Good. I'm going to do a handstand now, to cope. Don't watch. Watch a bit.
-> END

~ talk_devoted
if name:wren_featherfoot and approval.wren_featherfoot >= devoted and level >= 8
-> devoted
endif
-> END

~ devoted
Narrator: Wren comes and sits next to you on watch, which he never does; he hates watch. He's quiet for a long while.
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Master Sorrel used to say the last lesson is always who you are when the teacher's gone. I thought that was very deep. Now I think he just didn't want to write the last lesson.
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Thing is, the teacher's gone, and here I am, and I know who I am. Mostly. I'm the one who'd walk into that castle for you lot without a joke ready. That's new. That's terrifying.
* We'd do the same for you. -> devoted_same
* Have a joke ready anyway. -> devoted_joke

~ devoted_same
interject name:wren_featherfoot: I know. I've seen you. That's the worst part. I've got nobody to blame for this but all of you.
approve wren_featherfoot +3: You told me we'd do the same for you
-> devoted_end

~ devoted_joke
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Oh, I will. I've got a good one for Strahd. It's about his hair. I've been saving it.
approve wren_featherfoot +3: You told me to have a joke ready anyway
-> devoted_end

~ devoted_end
inspire name:wren_featherfoot: knew who he is with the teacher gone
-> END
